ed as  azerbaijani territory  these attacks are along  armenian communities along the the  border  inside armenia which would represent a  significant escalation uh in in  azerbaijan's  targeting  we're hearing that armenia's phoned a  number of world leaders  asking for help this morning is anyone  responding  well the key uh  actor here is russia uh uh prime  minister uh nicole pashanyan spoke with  uh russian president vladimir putin this  morning  asked for russia to intervene based on  the the mutual defense pact that the two  countries have  uh this has never been uh exercised in  the past because like i said all the the  fighting has gone on on  azerbaijani territory now that it's  spread apparently uh to armenian  territory this is going to be a big  question if the fighting continues  russia according to that treaty  would be obligated to come to armenia's  defense  of course russia in the last few days  has been  suffering its own military defeats in  ukraine and i think that that probably  explains why this offensive was launched  now  but anyway that's going to be the key  the key question is how russia responds  so far they've acknowledged armenia's  request for for assistance  but have not uh indicated how they're  going to respond  you mentioned ukraine does does all this  mean that we could see a second fully  fledged war in the post uh soviet world  uh well at this point it's really hard  to say i mean most of the times that  azerbaijan has escalated things it has  to do with pressuring armenia  uh to continue to carry out the terms of  the 2020 ceasefire  agreement or to work towards a  a comprehensive peace agreement so kind  of military pressure to get diplomatic  results i mean this is a big military  escalation  uh whether it's to continue to get more  diplomatic results or whether  they have some bigger intentions it's  too early to say so far  something we'll be watching closely  journalist joshua kuchera thank you so  much  you
 

